    "Cost": 4589181,
    "UIName": "Thunderer III MT",
    "Id": "vehicledef_THUNDERER_III",
    "Name": "Thunderer III MT",
    "Details": "Created by a Capellan Confederation design team, the Thunderer was rushed into production during the chaos of the 4th succession war. Originally intended as a heavy tank to anchor second line formations and support infantry, the tank made a name for itself as a capable sniper that could harass and kill Mechs. The MK3 Thunderer mounts 10.5 tons of stealth armour and is built around a 165 rated XL engine. A paired RAC/5 and Large Laser are mounted in the turret, along with a TAG, providing the Thunderer with the means to spot for allied artillery units. A hull mounted Anti Missile System  provides a modicum of defense against missiles.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 3/5 hexes / 90/150 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Vehicle Stealth Armor\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       215     30\n<b>Left</b>         135     30\n<b>Right</b>       135     30\n<b>Rear</b>        120     30\n<b>Turret</b>      200     30\n\n<b>Total</b>      805    150</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Improved Targeting - Long</color>",
    "Icon": "Zhukov"
  },
